and improving friendship.

01:12:16.000 --> 01:12:19.213
So to me I just think it
relates back in that way

01:12:19.213 --> 01:12:21.738
that like yeah I do
believe it's gonna happen

01:12:21.738 --> 01:12:25.320
and it's because we can't help ourselves.

01:12:25.320 --> 01:12:28.020
We're relational beings.

01:12:28.020 --> 01:12:30.630
- Yeah I have absolutely no doubt that

01:12:32.570 --> 01:12:35.850
these things that we bristle
at and we think are weird...

01:12:39.650 --> 01:12:43.040
Something like this Replika
thing and the nature,

01:12:43.040 --> 01:12:46.430
even the way that our kids
relate to AI differently

01:12:46.430 --> 01:12:48.820
than we do because it's just
they're growing up with it.

01:12:48.820 --> 01:12:49.890
- Right.

01:12:49.890 --> 01:12:51.893
- And as it gets more and more advanced,

01:12:53.227 --> 01:12:57.982
this is an inescapable,
inevitable part of our future

01:12:57.982 --> 01:13:01.740
and again, I don't think it's a bad thing.

01:13:01.740 --> 01:13:06.312
I think that if it takes away
from human relationships,

01:13:06.312 --> 01:13:08.810
then it could be a bad thing but I think

01:13:08.810 --> 01:13:10.820
that if it enhances human
relationships and I think

01:13:10.820 --> 01:13:13.283
if used correctly, it can.

01:13:15.110 --> 01:13:18.520
Maybe a good analogy to
this is just the internet

01:13:18.520 --> 01:13:21.130
in general, it's like,
the internet was supposed

01:13:21.130 --> 01:13:25.190
to represent this incredible connectivity

01:13:25.190 --> 01:13:28.160
between the entire world
and it has done that.

01:13:28.160 --> 01:13:31.140
The level of information and
the different perspectives,

01:13:31.140 --> 01:13:32.522
one of the reasons it's so difficult

01:13:32.522 --> 01:13:35.243
to maintain a close-minded,

01:13:36.504 --> 01:13:38.920
I'm right and everyone
else is wrong perspective

01:13:38.920 --> 01:13:41.950
in the year 2019 if you're
a connected individual is

01:13:41.950 --> 01:13:45.640
because unlike any time in
history, you have the ability

01:13:45.640 --> 01:13:48.610
to see other people's perspectives,

01:13:48.610 --> 01:13:50.720
to hear their perspectives
through the internet,

01:13:50.720 --> 01:13:54.650
whereas if you go back 30, 40 years,

01:13:54.650 --> 01:13:56.580
you could be isolated in
a community who thought

01:13:56.580 --> 01:13:58.620
the same way about every single thing

01:13:58.620 --> 01:14:00.100
and never have that perspective challenged

01:14:00.100 --> 01:14:01.840
at all and that's over.

01:14:01.840 --> 01:14:05.840
So interactivity, the
connectivity of the internet

01:14:05.840 --> 01:14:09.350
has brought people together
but at the same time,

01:14:09.350 --> 01:14:12.471
as we just saw with the way
the Russians got involved

01:14:12.471 --> 01:14:15.310
on Facebook and all the
things that were happening

01:14:15.310 --> 01:14:17.310
with the bots and our previous election,

01:14:18.180 --> 01:14:21.100
the country is more polarized
than it ever has been

01:14:21.100 --> 01:14:23.470
because of their connectivity,

01:14:23.470 --> 01:14:26.420
because of these filter
bubbles that everyone is in

01:14:26.420 --> 01:14:30.150
based on the way Facebook
works and the way Google works.

01:14:30.150 --> 01:14:33.110
And the way that you
get the search results

01:14:33.110 --> 01:14:35.720
that are catered to you
and your particular tastes.

01:14:35.720 --> 01:14:38.090
- Yeah and then I start to think

01:14:38.090 --> 01:14:40.453
if you have this robot friend,

01:14:43.000 --> 01:14:48.000
well, you can have an unhealthy
relationship with that robot

01:14:49.160 --> 01:14:51.470
just like you can with another person.

01:14:51.470 --> 01:14:56.470
And you can also, and what is the robot,

01:14:56.510 --> 01:14:58.370
what is the AI bringing
to the relationship?

01:14:58.370 --> 01:14:59.920
Are they innately good?

01:14:59.920 --> 01:15:02.524
Are they bad?

01:15:02.524 --> 01:15:06.990
Are they neutral and
is that even possible?

01:15:06.990 --> 01:15:09.250
It's like--
- Well I think ultimately

01:15:09.250 --> 01:15:11.620
what I'm saying is that--
- Difficult.

01:15:11.620 --> 01:15:15.850
- If this Replika, if this
AI enhances your relationship

01:15:15.850 --> 01:15:20.850
with your grandmother more
than if you didn't have access

01:15:20.860 --> 01:15:24.050
to this AI, it's good but
if now all of a sudden

01:15:24.050 --> 01:15:25.450
you're like you know
what, I don't need grandma

01:15:25.450 --> 01:15:28.870
because I've got this
bot, then it's a problem.

01:15:28.870 --> 01:15:30.940
Which kinda goes back
to just it's up to us

01:15:30.940 --> 01:15:32.840
in the way that we interact with this.

01:15:34.180 --> 01:15:39.180
- And the way we design
it and put parameters

01:15:39.400 --> 01:15:40.440
and boundaries on it.

01:15:40.440 --> 01:15:43.483
- But the answer is
not to be scared of it.

01:15:44.442 --> 01:15:47.170
I don't know how many times
we have to go through this.

01:15:47.170 --> 01:15:51.260
Being scared of the advance of technology

01:15:52.684 --> 01:15:56.060
and trying to stave it
off, it just doesn't work.

01:15:56.060 --> 01:15:58.650
These things happen,
all this stuff happens.

01:15:58.650 --> 01:16:01.140
- But being, I think--
- Being cautious.

01:16:01.140 --> 01:16:02.650
- Being scared--
- Cautious is good.

01:16:02.650 --> 01:16:04.010
- And checking out--

01:16:04.010 --> 01:16:05.360
- Yeah I'm talking about running from it.

01:16:05.360 --> 01:16:06.780
- You're not helping.

01:16:06.780 --> 01:16:08.240
But if you're afraid of certain things

01:16:08.240 --> 01:16:11.170
and then you're involved
to prevent those things

01:16:11.170 --> 01:16:13.090
I think that's absolutely necessary so--

01:16:13.090 --> 01:16:15.270
- Yeah we should be cautious
and we should be realistic

01:16:15.270 --> 01:16:17.700
about the potential but to check out--

01:16:17.700 --> 01:16:20.240
- Keep studying your
engineering and your ethics

01:16:21.500 --> 01:16:25.913
